.TH "RTCTRANSPORTSTATS.DTLSROLE" "3JS" "June 20, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCTransportStats.dtlsRole \- RTCTransportStats: dtlsRole property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]dtlsRole\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]RTCTransportStats\f[R] dictionary is a string that indicates the
role of the associated \f[CR]RTCPeerConnection\f[R] in the DTLS
negotiation.
.PP
Specifically, whether it acted like a server and listened for
connections, or like a client and initiated the connection, or that
negotiation has not yet started.
.SH VALUE
A string indicating the DTLS role.
This will be one of:
.TP
\f[B]client\f[R]
The peer initiated the DTLS handshake.
.TP
\f[B]server\f[R]
The peer waited for the DTLS handshake.
.TP
\f[B]unknown\f[R]
DTLS negotiation has not started.
